# One terminator per file, declared here rather than left to whatever `core.autocrlf` the
# machine happens to set (RK1132, and L6 applied to this repository's own tooling).
#
# The measurement that produced this line: 45 of the 56 package modules held CRLF in the
# working tree while 11 held LF, and eight test files held **both** — because the index is
# normalised to LF and some editors write CRLF back. Nothing renders differently and no diff
# is at stake; what it costs is that a scripted edit anchored on one terminator matches
# nothing in a file that uses the other, silently. That is RK1091's defect one layer down,
# and it stopped two patches in a single session.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's own detection for anything binary somebody adds later; `eol=lf`
# is what makes a **checkout** agree with the index on every platform, which is the half a
# per-machine setting cannot promise to a contributor who never set it.
* text=auto eol=lf
docs/ROADMAP.md merge=roadkeep
docs/CHANGELOG.md merge=roadkeep
docs/IMPROVEMENTS.md merge=roadkeep
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=roadkeep
